{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-03-06","source":"Senate","text":"Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry Subcommittee on Conservation, Forestry, Natural Resources, and Biotechnology. Hearings held. With printed Hearing: S.Hrg. 119-27.","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-01-28","source":"Senate","text":"Received in the Senate.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"H38310","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"Motion to reconsider laid on the table Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H37100","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 279 - 141 (Roll no. 25). (text: CR H321-333)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"8000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Passed/agreed to in House: On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 279 - 141 (Roll no. 25). (text: CR H321-333)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H346-347)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"POSTPONED PROCEEDINGS - At the conclusion of debate on H.R. 471, the Chair put the question on passage of the bill and by voice vote, announced that the ayes had prevailed. Mr. Peters demanded the yeas and nays and the Chair postponed further proceedings until a time to be announced.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H34400","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"The House adopted the amendments en gros as agreed to by the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H35000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H32600","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"The House rose from the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union to report H.R. 471.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H.Res. 53, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Carbajal amendment No. 2.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H.Res. 53, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Perry amendment No. 1.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"GENERAL DEBATE - The Committee of the Whole proceeded with one hour of general debate on H.R. 471.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H32400","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"The Speaker designated the Honorable Dale W. Strong to act as Chairman of the Committee.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H32020","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"House resolved itself into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union pursuant to H. Res. 53 and Rule XVIII.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 471 and S. 5. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 471 under a structured rule with one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit. Also, the resolution provides for consideration of S. 5 under a closed rule with one hour of general debate and one motion to commit.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2025-01-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 53. (consideration: CR H312-335)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L210","actionDate":"2025-01-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 53 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 471 and S. 5. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 471 under a structured rule with one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit. Also, the resolution provides for consideration of S. 5 under a closed rule with one hour of general debate and one motion to commit.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on Natural Resources, and in addition to the Committees on Agriculture, and Science, Space, and Technology, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on Natural Resources, and in addition to the Committees on Agriculture, and Science, Space, and Technology, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on Natural Resources, and in addition to the Committees on Agriculture, and Science, Space, and Technology, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-01-16","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-01-16","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/471","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"P00